REFERENCE MATERIAL

The runtime semantics implemented here — layer topology, MLA and compressed-KV
handling, the DSA index path, MoME state, the mHC merge, routing and the MoE
accumulation order — were determined by reading Huawei's published openPangu
model card, checkpoint configuration, and the openPangu-2.0-Infer inference
implementation, which is licensed under Apache-2.0. Specifically:

  components/omni-npu/src/omni_npu/v1/models/pangu/pangu_v2_moe.py
  components/omni-npu/src/omni_npu/v1/models/pangu/pangu_v2_moe_mtp.py
  components/omni-npu/src/omni_npu/attention/backends/{mla,dsa,mome}.py
  components/omni-cache/omni_cache/cache/prefill/mome_state_utils.py

No source from those files is copied into this repository. The code here is an
independent C++/CUDA implementation written against NVIDIA hardware, and its
kernels, memory layout, quantisation handling and scheduling differ throughout.
The reference is credited because the behaviour it defines is Huawei's work.

